{"words": [{"text": "وَٱبْتَلُوا۟", "translation": "And test"}, {"text": "ٱلْيَتَـٰمَىٰ", "translation": "the orphans"}, {"text": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translation": "until"}, {"text": "إِذَا", "translation": "[when]"}, {"text": "بَلَغُوا۟", "translation": "they reach[ed]"}, {"text": "ٱلنِّكَاحَ", "translation": "(the age of) marriage"}, {"text": "فَإِنْ", "translation": "then if"}, {"text": "ءَانَسْتُم", "translation": "you perceive"}, {"text": "مِّنْهُمْ", "translation": "in them"}, {"text": "رُشْدًۭا", "translation": "sound judgement"}, {"text": "فَٱدْفَعُوٓا۟", "translation": "then deliver"}, {"text": "إِلَيْهِمْ", "translation": "to them"}, {"text": "أَمْوَٰلَهُمْ ۖ", "translation": "their wealth"}, {"text": "وَلَا", "translation": "And (do) not"}, {"text": "تَأْكُلُوهَآ", "translation": "eat it"}, {"text": "إِسْرَافًۭا", "translation": "extravagantly"}, {"text": "وَبِدَارًا", "translation": "and hastily"}, {"text": "أَن", "translation": "(fearing) that"}, {"text": "يَكْبَرُوا۟ ۚ", "translation": "they will grow up"}, {"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "And whoever"}, {"text": "كَانَ", "translation": "is"}, {"text": "غَنِيًّۭا", "translation": "rich"}, {"text": "فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ ۖ", "translation": "then he should refrain"}, {"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "and whoever"}, {"text": "كَانَ", "translation": "is"}, {"text": "فَقِيرًۭا", "translation": "poor"}, {"text": "فَلْيَأْكُلْ", "translation": "then let him eat (of it)"}, {"text": "بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ ۚ", "translation": "in a fair manner"}, {"text": "فَإِذَا", "translation": "Then when"}, {"text": "دَفَعْتُمْ", "translation": "you deliver"}, {"text": "إِلَيْهِمْ", "translation": "to them"}, {"text": "أَمْوَٰلَهُمْ", "translation": "their wealth"}, {"text": "فَأَشْهِدُوا۟", "translation": "then take witnesses"}, {"text": "عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ", "translation": "on them"}, {"text": "وَكَفَىٰ", "translation": "And is sufficient"}, {"text": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "حَسِيبًۭا", "translation": "(as) a Reckoner"}], "sahih": "And test the orphans [in their abilities] until they reach marriageable age. Then if you perceive in them sound judgement, release their property to them. And do not consume it excessively and quickly, [anticipating] that they will grow up. And whoever, [when acting as guardian], is self-sufficient should refrain [from taking a fee]; and whoever is poor - let him take according to what is acceptable. Then when you release their property to them, bring witnesses upon them. And sufficient is Allāh as Accountant."}